  "dom_id": "step-q141481",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/5c7723e43696fac78180663115c50ed76c81c8841e3a99eb26122860f798dcc4.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{RS}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TR}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RP}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QP}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$",
  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $P$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=\\overset{\\to }{QT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RP}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/da5a61cf57c3ffcf82b693b8738334bc840a13b5f34068858e20453906d1b6f2.png)\n\n  \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TR}=c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{RP}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/c3cb5fabcbd664b0e5eef879cf54f7a5b5d0f187c2f3d68a71d3c91b972005e3.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QP} & =\\overset{\\to }{QT}+\\overset{\\to }{TR}+\\overset{\\to }{RP} \\\\  & =a+c+d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
